ons to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions, with a 0.2% error rate. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14604, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S2MWR6PaeXxHBGn9oFQCaS", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14604, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S2MWR6PaeXxHBGn9oFQCaS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18393, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in all three regions.\n- **Check afterwards:** The service reports healthy on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident INC-0001:** It says what failed, what I rolled back to and the current state. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone deploys it again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LWaQGMScxpEXCFYr7mHYq3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01XePzDRBijUqfQp3H1QwVYi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01JscvFyGwVD4a9HXUL1esWk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011qkLKx6dwZEmHZwpko6RjU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VTotLXQH76aFJREYohnsfP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01S2MWR6PaeXxHBGn9oFQCaS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the latest deploy of v2.3.1 (seq 3), checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. We rolled checkout-api back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, the service reports healthy on v2.3.0 in all regions, with a 0.2% error rate. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. Its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy in staging.\n- **Rollback:** I picked v2.3.0 because it's the most recent release that was healthy in production. It's now running in all three regions.\n- **Check afterwards:** The service reports healthy on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident INC-0001:** It says what failed, what I rolled back to and the current state. It also says the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone deploys it again.", "type": "text"}]}]}